From: liberodark <liberodark@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: spacemit: k3: enable PCIe on CoM260-IFX

The CoM260-IFX (BPI-SM10) boots from an NVMe drive on PCIe port A, with
the same x4 wiring as the Pico-ITX. Enable the first PCIe root complex
on this board.

Rebased on v7.3-rc1: the PHY node and the PCIe host nodes now come from
upstream, so only the board level enablement is left here.

Rebased on v7.4-rc1: upstream now enables the combo PHY on this board
with mux 0x14 (PCIe A x4, PCIe C lane 0 in USB mode for the VL817 hub on
usb3b). Do not override it with the Pico-ITX value 0x11 any more, which
would take lane 2 away from the USB 3 hub; PCIe A x4 is the same in both.

Signed-off-by: liberodark <liberodark@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts
index fadcf28389be..6bfd1a9e75b9 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260-ifx.dts
@@ -129,3 +129,15 @@ &sdhci0 {
 	sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&pcie0_rc {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&pcie0_0_cfg>;
+	num-lanes = <4>;
+	status = "okay";
+
+	pcie@0 {
+		phys = <&combophy 0 PHY_TYPE_PCIE>,
+		       <&combophy 1 PHY_TYPE_PCIE>;
+	};
+};
